      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-31T08:53:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In theory, the containsKey method should also be used, but code checking reminds me of the following issue:\n\nThe code employs a non-atomic check-then-act sequence on the ConcurrentHashMap, which may lead to a NullPointerException. If another thread concurrently deletes the entry after containsKey() returns true, mAllUsersInfo.get(userId) could return null, resulting in a null pointer exception when accessing .mAccept. In AOSP system services, such a crash may interrupt biometric operations.\n\nSo I changed it to this writing style to avoid it",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 116,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "0a6e1f7fa08ab9ba58a3f0586961f154b48c1eac",
